                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b][i]Jack B. Nimble[/i] is a competent one-button endless runner with a good price point.[/b] The pixel art is very well done, and the whole thing has a strong 'one more run' appeal. While I have some nitpicks, overall this is easily worth the small asking price for fans of the genre.\n\n[b]Pros:[/b]\n+Very fun 'one more run' endless runner\n+Nice pixel art\n+Some fun (mostly) cosmetic unlockables\n+Scoring system is easy to understand and works well\n\n[b]Cons:[/b]\n-While only one button is needed for the core gameplay, for some reason I need a mouse to navigate menus\n-For being quite a simple game, the optimization is fairly poor for lower end machines\n- While there are unlockables, I wish there were more (and more functional ones, too)\n-Has a bit of an identity crisis; it begins with a strong [i]Castlevania[/i] theme but quickly deviates widely\n\n[b]You know what you are getting into with this one.[/b] It's fun. Give it a go.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1533134465,
